and we're saying good night.

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:32.434
And I said, "Chris --"
You know, you guys don't know,

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:35.767
Chris is a mentor,
friend, inspiration.

00:05:35.767 --> 00:05:38.467
But he's a large part
of the reason that I am

00:05:38.467 --> 00:05:40.033
where I am today in my career

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:42.033
just from his advice,
his insight, et cetera.

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:45.234
And he's my G.O.A.T.,
like, he's my guy.

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:48.501
And I wanted him to feel
that and experience

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:49.968
the world of understanding

00:05:49.968 --> 00:05:51.801
of how I feel about him
in front of that audience.

00:05:51.801 --> 00:05:53.367
So I gave him the goat
and I said,

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:54.934
"Please give my guy
his flowers."

00:05:54.934 --> 00:05:57.501
And they stood up,
screamed, loved.

00:05:57.501 --> 00:05:59.167
He almost cried.
He almost broke down and cried

00:05:59.167 --> 00:06:00.534
